   176	
   177	### Phase 1b implementation notes
   178	
   179	| Revision | Reason |
   180	|---|---|
   181	| P1 and P2 compare .30 with .50. P3 compares the best tested setting for each arm. | The archived paired directions motivate empirical confirmation. The theoretical window does not determine how end-to-end gain changes with ρ. |
   182	| Use exact per-contrast α = .05/3 and equal tails for P1–P2. For P3, apply a Bonferroni rectangle at the same family level over the twelve arm-by-ρ crossings after paired U/G averaging. | The joint rectangle covers the crossings before grid minimization. Each arm's minimum uses the minima of its lower and upper endpoints. The contrast then subtracts opposite endpoints. |
   183	| Keep paired censor bounds and report V1, V4, and below-.30 differences descriptively. Use the simultaneous crossing rectangle for optimum sets. | Censoring can leave a decisive endpoint. An optimum set retains ρ whenever its lower endpoint is no higher than the smallest upper endpoint. The report gives whether all CD-compatible ratios are below all F0-compatible ratios. |
   184	| Stratify mechanism readouts by exact scenario, ρ, and SNR. | Rescues and harms use the trigger count. First-edit class shares use all accepted first global edits, including other moves. Common-pair score shares use only triggers with a legal pair. |
   185	| Define the scene average as the arithmetic mean of the two scenario crossings. | The reported dB statistic gives equal weight to the U and G crossing estimates. |
   186	| Resample the four archived scenario/ρ curves using 400 and 600 physical-frame draws from the same 400-frame cohort. | This projects precision under the archived error curves and SNR brackets. The P3 projection covers a two-setting minimum over .30/.50 and uses the same twelve-crossing tail allocation as the six-setting analysis. The other four settings are needed to estimate the six-setting precision. |
   187	
   188	The first-edit labels follow the admission-law integer-delay convention. A co-delay addition at a surviving fitted delay is the structural phantom proxy. The report separately counts proxy events where the true channel contains multiple paths at that delay. A new fitted delay counts as a recovery when the true channel contains it and the entering support lacks it. This label measures recovered delay, without requiring exact Doppler.
   189	
   190	For the common-pair readout, the strongest occupied and strongest missing true path define two delays. Use the fitted anchor closest in Doppler to the occupied true path. Select the weakest fitted replacement slot that keeps that anchor and admits both types of candidate. Use the nearest legal bank Doppler to the anchor for the co-delay candidate and to the missing true Doppler for the recovery candidate. Both arms score the same legal slot and pair on the same entering F0 support. Lower objective wins. Ties and unavailable pairs are counted separately. This readout reuses the existing first-exchange scores and makes no additional receiver calls.
   191	
   192	
   193	### Phase 1b qualification and frame decision
   194	
   195	| Check | Evidence |
   196	|---|---|
   197	| Archived parity | F0/CD and replayed A2 matched all 1,976 triggers. The mechanism summary includes all 13,600 archived keys. |
   198	| Smoke parity and repeatability | All 32 keys reproduced the Phase 1 receiver outputs and repeated the new diagnostics. |
   199	| Synthetic tests | 13 analysis and 10 mechanism tests passed, covering decisive one-sided intervals, censoring, ties, the six-setting tail allocation and diagnostic denominators. |
   200	
   201	The [qualification receipt](out/phase1b/qualification.json) records exact producing source hashes, inputs, and timing. The original Phase 1 sources are at commit `8c92399c`. The [mechanism receipt](out/phase1b/mechanism.json) gives scenario/ρ/SNR counts and shares for both arms. On the archived triggered keys, A2 rescued 276/1,976 and CD rescued 657/1,976. Both had zero harms. Among the 1,519 shared legal-pair triggers, the structural phantom candidate won 1,458 for A2 and 23 for CD. These are retrospective diagnostic counts. The [raw rows](out/phase1b/qualification.json) are retained on deinlab at `/data/guoyikun/00inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/rho_sweep_20261119/out/phase1b/archive-mechanism-rows.jsonl`, SHA-256 `7f0495670c59c560097b7d0f437a40af8ff2afec117d8acd348ce7c58926bd95`.
   202	
   203	The [precision receipt](out/phase1b/precision.json) gives the following projected 98.33% intervals. Every half-width is unbounded because the archival SNR floor leaves one endpoint censored. The finite endpoints improve at 600 draws. P3 covers the two-setting archive proxy.
   204	
   205	| Contrast | 400 frames, interval (dB) | 400 half-width | 600 frames, interval (dB) | 600 half-width |
   206	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   207	| P1 | [0.596, +∞) | ∞ | [0.693, +∞) | ∞ |
   208	| P2 | (−∞, −0.888] | ∞ | (−∞, −0.928] | ∞ |
   209	| P3 (.30/.50 proxy) | [0.393, +∞) | ∞ | [0.545, +∞) | ∞ |
   210	
   211	The P1 precision condition favors more frames. The full grid projects to **8.314 core-hours at 400 frames and 12.472 at 600**, including the 1.3× margin and the mechanism logging. §7 therefore retains **400 frames, 5400–5799**, all 13 SNR values including 3 and 12 dB, and 62,400 keys. The conditional 5800–5999 audit is unnecessary with this frame decision. Phase 1b used **0.540 core-hours** on archived and smoke keys. The selected frames remain blind.
