codex
**Revise two things before freezing: the candidate generator and the Stage A decision rule.** Round 0 is the right injection point. The biggest risk is that the reported 83.2% recovery measures visibility with truth-assisted scoring, while Stage B needs a receiver that can choose eight entries from observations alone.

1. **Where support is fixed.** Round 0 groups pilot atoms by delay, keeps up to eight distinct delays by summed gain energy, and takes the strongest atom at each retained delay as its Doppler center. Round 1 receives only those survivors, so it can refine their Dopplers and gains but cannot recover a discarded delay. CODELAY can subsequently replace up to two slots on its own global grid if the round-1 parity check fails. Each arm must pass **its own** round-1 state and trigger to CODELAY. Neither downstream stage needs the discarded candidate list. [twofft.py:87](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/sp_afdm_native_joint_20260921/src/twofft.py:87) · [native_twofft.py:27](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/sp_afdm_native_joint_20260921/src/native_twofft.py:27) · [phase1.py:62](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/rho_sweep_20261119/phase1.py:62) · [e1_driver.py:212](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/tf_cstate_e1_20261017/e1_driver.py:212)

2. **Stage A and precision.** A is an optimistic reference for initialization. It supplies both true delays and rounded true Dopplers, which matters because refinement searches only ±0.75 around each center. An A gain therefore cannot be attributed to delay recovery alone. The iterative decoder and conditional exchanges also give no guarantee that A bounds B’s final frame error rate (FER). Keep 0.3 dB as the minimum worthwhile gain and \(\rho\le .20\) as the operating target. The old paired .25-minus-.30 crossing difference was just **0.057 dB** (95% interval **−0.159 to +0.263**), and .20, .25, .30 and .40 were all compatible baseline optima. A point-estimated winning \(\rho\) is too unstable for a stop rule. [twofft.py:102](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/sp_afdm_native_joint_20260921/src/twofft.py:102) · [RESULTS.md:103](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/rho_sweep_20261119/out/main_20261119/RESULTS.md:103) · [RESULTS.md:141](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/rho_sweep_20261119/out/main_20261119/RESULTS.md:141)

3. **Which arm passes candidates through.** B-rank guarantees admission for its highest-ranked distinct delays. B-union gives weak candidates another chance to lose on pilot energy and changes the least-squares fit for incumbent atoms too. A simpler comparison keeps seven baseline slots and challenges the eighth with the strongest new autocorrelation delay, using the same observable Doppler-center rule for both. This tests whether one proposal adds value. Eight final slots equalize downstream capacity, while candidate generation and any enlarged fit still cost extra. [design.md:15](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/.trellis/tasks/11-21-data-pilot-fer/design.md:15)

4. **What the hypotheses predict.** Final FER alone cannot separate poor initial parameter estimates from failed decoder feedback. On the same frames, record missing path power, power-weighted Doppler error, and decoded information-bit errors after rounds 0 and 1 and after exchange. This shows whether a recovered path improves the first decode and whether that improvement survives feedback. These are diagnostic associations. In earlier triggered frames with exactly correct final delays, 69/1,580 still failed at low pilot power. [READOUT.md:6](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/lowpilot_support_right_20261120/READOUT.md:6)

5. **Two freeze changes.**
   - **Freeze an observable candidate selector.** Rank actual local peaks before consulting truth, resolve mirrors, deduplicate delays, and enforce the declared budget. Score truth afterward, both before and after eight-slot admission, against actual baseline misses. The existing probe masks true anchor-pair neighborhoods and searches around each true weak path. Its 83.2% denominator is a matched-filter proxy. Reproducing that number is the wrong implementation gate. [calc2.py:55](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/data_autocorr_acq_20261121/calc2.py:55) · [READOUT2.md:26](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/data_autocorr_acq_20261121/READOUT2.md:26)
   - **Freeze a paired low-pilot headroom gate.** Compare the best baseline crossing on the comparison grid, including .25, with A’s best crossing at \(\rho\le .20\). Recompute both minima in each paired physical-frame bootstrap draw using decoded-frame failures and preserving censoring. Continue if the 95% lower gain bound exceeds 0.3 dB, stop for futility if the upper bound falls below it, and label overlap inconclusive. That answers whether low-pilot operation can beat the baseline by a useful margin. Report the optimum-\(\rho\) set separately. [PROTOCOL.md:134](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/rho_sweep_20261119/PROTOCOL.md:134) · [analysis.py:123](/Users/guoyikun/Downloads/share/claode_birain/my-vault/00_Inbox/AFDM-channel-estimation/experiments/rho_sweep_20261119/analysis.py:123)
